.vitest-attachments/
# Generated by Next on every command, and it OSCILLATES: `next dev` writes the .next/dev/types
# import, `next build` writes the .next/types one, so a tracked copy flips back and forth and
# shows as a modified file to whoever ran the other command last. It carries a do-not-edit
# header and nothing in CI reads it before a build (docs#lint dependsOn build), so it is an
# artifact, not a source file — and in a repo with drift laws, a tracked file that rewrites
# itself by command is a standing false positive.
apps/docs/next-env.d.ts
